// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3151690920" "Mr. G's New Card"
// tDetailString :
"P3281642500" "Mr. G gave you a card with his new information on it. It makes you think that you might've found...<br><br><b>Praetoria's Hidden Treasure</b><br><br>You found out that Arachnos was staging an operation to loot Praetoria before the Hamidon destroyed it. You snuck in through the DESTINY portal to try to take something for yourself.<br><br>You found a badly injured Mr. G beneath the streets of Imperial City. He revealed that he was the villain, Doppelganger. Mr. G had plans to build an army of clones to take over Primal Earth and Praetoria, but that plan was destroyed by Praetor Sinclair.<br><br>Mr. G offered a deal to you - if you saved his life, he would serve you in Primal Earth. You agreed and warned Mr. G that he would be dead if he even thought about betraying your alliance."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - FlashbackLeft 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - TamiBaker 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KnewTami Text :
"P264255384" "<color orange>You see Tami Baker and remember your time working with her in Imperial City. It looks like she was killed recently. You notice she wasn't killed by the Devouring Earth. She has several slices across her body that look to be the work of a heavy bladed weapon, almost certainly a sword, and by the depth of the wounds, probably a katana</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page DidntKnowTami Text :
"P3031927099" "<color orange>You see the body of a civilian on the ground. It looks like she was killed recently. You notice she wasn't killed by the Devouring Earth. She has several slices across her body that look to be the work of a heavy bladed weapon, almost certainly a sword, and by the depth of the wounds, probably a katana</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - TamiBakerClone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KnewTami Text :
"P675406818" "<color orange>You see... another Tami Baker? She is also dead, killed by someone wielding a katana. What exactly is going on?</color>"
// Page DidntKnowTami Text :
"P4053628030" "<color orange>You see the body of the same woman that was outside of the lab. She is also dead, killed by someone wielding a katana. What exactly is going on?</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ProjectPhoenix 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KnewPhoenix Text :
"P1874975667" "<color orange>You see the body of a member of Project Phoenix. However, you remember dealing with the last members of that project with Praetor Sinclair. How is this person here?</color>"
// Page DidntKnowPhoenix Text :
"P3604182428" "<color orange>You see the body of what appears to be a ninja. Their wounds indicate they were killed by a katana.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Clone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3843789940" "<color orange>You see... yourself! How is that possible? The clone factory you had taken control of was destroyed by Protean. Yet, here you see dead clones of yourself scattered throughout the room. What is the meaning of all this? Who is using you in this manner?</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Sinclair 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P57870873" "<color orange>You see the dead body of Praetor Sinclair. His wounds are severe; it looks like he went down fighting nearly every single being that's within this lab. He has other wounds as well, which must have been from his fight in the Magisterium.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrG 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page DidLeonardDidMrG Text :
"P1542403869" "<color orange>Mr. G slowly looks up at you. He's badly injured. He laughs, shaking his head.</color><br><br>Quite interesting... that we should meet again, {HeroName}. Yes, quite interesting... urgh...! As you can... see... I've found myself in a bit of a situation...<br><br>Hah... here I thought Sinclair... couldn't fight <i>all</i> my clones... it looks like I was wrong."
// Answer Text :
"P2116414448" "What is the meaning of this, Mr. G? Tell me -everything-."
// Page DidLeonardDidMrGTellMeEverything Text :
"P27242569" "I suppose... I'm in no position to lie... no... no position to lie... no position. Hah... where to begin...<br><br>Have you heard of <color red>Doppelganger</color>? I'm sure you've heard of... Protean. Protean is Primal Earth's version of Doppelganger. That would... hah... happen to be me. Surprise, eh...? I was the one... who trained Sinclair. I assumed... I would be the one who killed him, too, though I have grown... old, unlike Protean.<br><br>The clones... ah... yes... that would be another story."
// Answer Text :
"P2823587863" "Keep talking."
// Page DidLeonardDidMrGKeepTalking Text :
"P3210486198" "Yes... well... I had a dream, {HeroName}. I realized... a clone of myself... would have my abilities. If I could control the clones... I could be anywhere... and everywhere. Tami Baker, my secretary, she was the first prototype. As you can see, I made several... she wasn't perfect... heh... she was even killed a few times by the Resistance, <i>quite</i> annoying.<br><br>I cloned the members of Project Phoenix before Sinclair... disposed of them. And... as you can see, <i>you</i> were the final step.<br><br>I was... working with Protean... before he abandoned me. He was the one... who sent me the data on... your cloning matrix. I would've made an army from you... {HeroName}... one that would've conquered Praetoria and Primal Earth...yes, conquered it quite nicely.<br><br>... Obviously that has been... foiled. Sinclair sought me out... in his last moments, believed he could try to... deliver some justice upon me, but I showed him, showed him what... I could still do."
// Answer Text :
"P2434142707" "Now that just leaves what I do with you, Mr. G."
// Page DidLeonard Text :
"P3942972862" "<color orange>The old man in the suit slowly looks up at you. He's badly injured. The man laughs, shaking his head.</color><br><br>Ah... {HeroName}. You're the... original... aren't you? Here I did not think... you and I would ever meet for quite some time, quite some time.<br><br>My name is... urgh... my name is <color yellow>Mr. G</color>. As you can... see... I've found myself in a bit of a situation...<br><br>Hah... here I thought Sinclair... couldn't fight <i>all</i> my clones... it looks like I was wrong."
// Answer Text :
"P295064989" "What happened to you? To Tami? What's going on?"
// Page DidMrGTellMeEverything Text :
"P3300315875" "I suppose... I'm in no position to lie... no... no position to lie indeed. Hah... where to begin...<br><br>Have you heard of <color red>Doppelganger</color>? I'm sure you've heard of... Protean. He is Primal Earth's version of Doppelganger. That would... hah... happen to be me. Surprise, eh...? I was the one... who trained Sinclair. I assumed... I would be the one who killed him, too, though I have grown... old, unlike Protean.<br><br>The clones... ah... yes... that would be another story."
// Page DidMrGKeepTalking Text :
"P420930044" "Yes... well... I had a dream, {HeroName}. I realized... a clone of myself... would have all my abilities. If I could control the clones... I could be anywhere... and everywhere. Tami Baker, my secretary, she was the first prototype. As you can see, I made several... she wasn't perfect... heh... she was even killed a few times by the Resistance, <i>quite</i> annoying.<br><br>I cloned the members of Project Phoenix before Sinclair... disposed of them. I would have made... an army... eventually... ruled Praetoria from the shadows...<br><br>Obviously, that project has been... shattered. Sinclair sought me out... in his last moments, believed he could try to... deliver some justice upon me, but I showed him, showed him what... I could still do."
// Page DidNothing Text :
"P3063825504" "<color orange>The old man in the suit slowly looks up at you. He's badly injured. The man laughs, shaking his head.</color><br><br>Ah... {HeroName}. I've... heard a bit about you.<br><br>My name is... urgh... my name is <color yellow>Mr. G</color>. As you can... see... I've found myself in a bit of a situation...<br><br>Hah... here I thought Sinclair... couldn't fight <i>all</i> my clones... it looks like I was wrong."
// Answer Text :
"P2673548875" "What exactly is going on? What were you planning?"
// Page WhatToDoWithG Text :
"P1689428007" "I have... a proposal... if you would hear me out. I can be... quite useful to you... quite useful.<br><br>I know of... some powerful assets that were taken by the Vanguard. I am also... quite good... at getting my hands on... information.<br><br>I can help you... with your plots... and schemes... gather information that you need. I can even suggest... one for you... which involves recovering criminals of... Praetoria... that Vanguard... has arrested.<br><br>They would all be under... your command... owing you a debt... we would all work... to help you with your... plots. I have... a small warehouse... in St. Martial... that we could use.<br><br>My own plots are over... {HeroName}... and I don't believe... I will ever fully recover from my wounds. Just help me... teleport out of here... and I'll be in your debt."
// Answer Text :
"P90670366" "Alright, Mr. G, but if you betray me, this is -over-. I'll see you in the Martial."
// Page Finish Text :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrGDelivery 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Flashback Text :
"P2964854000" "Ah... you have no idea how good it feels to... well... not be <i>dying</i>, yes, not dying.<br><br>In my short time back, very short, I've done some digging around, and I do believe I've found some information that can be of use to you. Shall we begin, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P1639332539" "Let's get to work. (Exit Flashback)"
// Answer Text :
"P2840620893" "Let's get to work."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1980738185" "<color orange>The clues were subtle at first. The number of plans that Arachnos had started to dwindle and they weren't sending out as many operatives on foreign assignments as they used to. Arachnos seemed to be concentrating on internal affairs, as if they were gearing up for something big. They were conducting numerous deals and more than a few raids on war materials to bolster their armories’ stockpiles. And then there was the research being done about the Devouring Earth. Disturbing reports that covered not only how to combat them, but also methods of controlling them.<br><br>The final piece of the puzzle came in when one of your contacts let slip that Arachnos was trying to figure out how to correctly deal amiably with the Carnival of Light and recruit displaced members of the Resistance. That's when it all fell into place! Arachnos must have been planning some sort of attack on Praetoria, but only <i>after</i> Cole was defeated.<br><br>You heard along the grapevine that Recluse staged a massive attack to bring down Tyrant himself, but that his armies were wiped out. It seems Recluse knew all along he wasn't going to defeat Tyrant - he was simply using this as a distraction while his army created another portal to sneak into Praetoria and loot the city of every scrap of useful information and technology they could get their hands on!"
// AcceptString :
"P3204924605" "(Ponder for a moment...)"
// SendOffString :
"P1848035501" "<color orange>You have it on good authority that Arachnos is finishing up their looting of Praetoria in Grandville. They're utilizing the DESTINY portal to travel to and from the area. The place should be in enough chaos from troops going back and forth that you could slip into the portal and investigate Praetoria yourself.<br><br>If Praetoria is collapsing, you should at least see what you can take from it before the Hamidon completely devours everything! You're not sure what you'll find, but you can't pass up this opportunity of discovering something interesting."
// TaskTitle :
"P3468396486" "<color deepskyblue>Praetoria's Hidden Treasure</color>"

